WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
What other kinds of foods would be beneficial from an epigenetic point of view?

00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:10,160
Well, more so what foods are probably best to stay away from a genetic point of view.

00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:14,080
And certainly with any cancer, you're trying to limit growth.

00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:20,480
So then you look at what foods stimulate growth pathways, metabolic pathways,

00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:24,640
and the first one that you should probably consider is dairy products.

00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:32,080
So dairy, I wouldn't say dairy is necessarily a cause of cancer per se, but it certainly

00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:34,960
is a stimulant to growth factors.

00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:44,800
You try to explain to people what is dairy for its milk, for a baby, for a 60 pound cow,

00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:50,160
to grow up to be a 1,200 pound cow. We certainly don't want to be adding growth factors.

00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:55,280
And I show in videos different men of the metabolic pathways to get them to understand that

00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:00,560
stimulates the caross pathway, which is a growth pathway. To get them to understand the

00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:07,840
technical side of that, but staying away from things that will stimulate growth of the cancer.

00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:13,760
So then we talk about from a dietary standpoint, cancer needs a fuel source.

00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:19,600
So whereas dairy is not necessarily a fuel source, it's a growth stimulator.

00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:24,960
But what is a fuel source of a cancer? It could be fed mainly directly through the pathway

00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:31,920
called glycolysis, which is how we break down glucose. So sugar should probably be something

00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:39,440
that all cancer patients should refrain from. But there are certain people that their cancer

00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:45,120
is stimulated completely off glycolysis, or that's the main source of fuel we could say.

00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:51,440
And then there's other people that their cancer currently is fueled off of amino acid,

00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:59,200
gobbling up amino acids, and that is the fuel source, lysine, and methionate, and glutamine.

00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:08,000
So those people should limit animal products like meat. That should be the main thing that they

00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,920
limit, not that they should be eating a bunch of carbohydrates, but they really have to limit

00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:19,920
protein sources, and typically it's animal protein sources, what we found.

00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:28,240
So it can vary. Some people really should be eating some animal proteins, and some people should not

00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:33,520
be eating any animal proteins. Probably every cancer across the board should stay away from dairy.

00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:38,480
Every cancer across the board should stay away from glucose, sugar, sucrose,

00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:44,880
has really no nutritional value. But some people don't need to stay away from fruit,

00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:53,440
and vegetable juicy, which could be high in glucose breakdown, but has all these other nutritional

00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:58,480
values. And if their cancer isn't fed directly through glycolysis, that's where juicy can be very

00:02:58,480 --> 00:03:06,480
beneficial for those people. So it does vary from person to person, not so much cancer to cancer,

00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:12,800
but person to person on the fuel source of that cancer. And you determine this through the DNA testing?

00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:25,520
You could get hints through the DNA testing, yes. Dr. Gonzalez and Dr. William Kelly did question

00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,040
here. Testing, metabolic testing, they called it. We do kinesiology testing as well to help determine that.

00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:42,560
A person not having any access to any of those things could look at how they feel after they eat

00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:49,600
those things. So if I juice, I don't feel as well when I'm juicing, or if I don't eat some meat,

00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:55,520
I don't feel well at all. Those are some hints that you could gather for what is possibly

00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:01,440
causing your cancer growth. Certainly, if you have a tumor that's visible and palpable,

00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:09,520
you can tell sometimes when what you're eating is adverse to the cancer. So there's different ways

00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:16,640
that you can tell what's currently feeding your cancer, but you want to try to cut off that pathway

00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,720
as much as possible.

